# Dialogue Designer — Build & Deploy

When ANY `.lua` file under `memories/DialogueEngine/Designer/` is modified, you MUST run the build script and copy the output to the Roblox Studio plugins folder before finishing:

```python
import subprocess, shutil, os
os.chdir("memories/DialogueEngine/Designer")
subprocess.run(["node", "build-rbxmx.cjs"], check=True)
plugins_dir = os.path.join(os.environ["LOCALAPPDATA"], "Roblox", "Plugins")
shutil.copy2("DialogueDesigner.rbxmx", os.path.join(plugins_dir, "DialogueDesigner.rbxmx"))
```

Or as two shell one-liners from `memories/DialogueEngine/Designer/`:

```bash
node build-rbxmx.cjs
python -c "import shutil,os; shutil.copy2('DialogueDesigner.rbxmx', os.path.join(os.environ['LOCALAPPDATA'],'Roblox','Plugins','DialogueDesigner.rbxmx'))"
```

This rebuilds the `.rbxmx` plugin bundle and deploys it so Studio picks up changes on next restart/reload.
